  "findings": [],
  "resolved_findings": [
    {
      "id": "P07-C01",
      "status": "resolved",
      "title": "Deleted registry ancestors were reclaimed while child handles retained tombstones",
      "files": [
        "kernel/src/persistence/config.rs",
        "kernel/src/persistence/codec.rs"
      ],
      "reproduction": "Create Parent and Parent\\Child, retain both handles, delete the child then parent, and flush. Both deletions succeeded but catalog serialization returned Corrupt until the child handle closed.",
      "resolution": "Retain deleted ancestry while any descendant or handle requires it; reclaim deleted keys leaf-first. Decode accepts consistent deleted ancestry and rejects live descendants below deleted ancestors.",
      "verified": "The original independent reproduction now flushes successfully before and after either handle closes. Project regressions exercise all six close orders of three levels, same-name recreation, unrelated settings, real journal commits/remounts, cold-mount tombstones and malformed live descendants. The final actual persist-save guest serializes deleted parent/child ancestry before closing each handle.",
      "before": "reports/runs/critic-p07/namespace-probe.log",
      "after": "reports/runs/critic-p07/namespace-probe-fixed.log"
    },
    {
      "id": "P07-C02",
      "status": "resolved",
      "title": "The raw journal auditor accepted contradictory valid-checksum mirror generations",
      "files": [
        "tools/xtask/src/persistence/journal.rs"
      ],
      "reproduction": "Independently checksum-valid checkpoint pairs (0,2), (1,0) and (9,0) were accepted by the host auditor while guest recovery rejected them.",
      "resolution": "The host auditor now enforces the same allowed generation/state relation as guest recovery, with exact same-state mirror equality and nonwrapping adjacent-generation rules.",
      "verified": "All three original contradictory pairs now reject. A separate arithmetic/state oracle matched both the guest journal and raw auditor in 392 cases, including both mirror slot orders and exhaustion boundaries. The project also tests its 17-row relation matrix in both orders.",
      "before": "reports/runs/critic-p07/auditor-probe.log",
      "after": "reports/runs/critic-p07/auditor-probe-fixed.log"
    },
    {
      "id": "P07-C03",
      "status": "resolved",
      "title": "Mixed-slash UNC prefixes resolved as local C paths",
      "files": [
        "kernel/src/persistence/path.rs"
      ],
      "reproduction": "Forward-slash and mixed-separator two-separator prefixes opened the local Users path, although canonical backslash UNC was rejected.",
      "resolution": "Ordinary Windows paths reject all four leading slash/backslash pairs before local-root resolution, while the explicit supported extended-prefix policy remains separate.",
      "verified": "The original public-API probe rejects all four UNC separator pairs with Unsupported. Project tests include CreateAlways nonmutation and the final guest rejects the same negative corpus against its persistent note.",
      "before": "reports/runs/critic-p07/path-probe.log",
      "after": "reports/runs/critic-p07/path-probe-fixed.log",
      "primary_reference": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/fileio/maximum-file-path-limitation"
    }
  ],
  "verification": [
    "Read AGENTS, relevant master sections 23-26,40,105,107,109,139, the selected phase ledger, status/handoff, journal and persistent-namespace contracts and associated ADRs. Reviewed the complete journal, ext2 truncate/unlink integration, namespace/security/path/config/codec, shared device lifetime, actual guest diagnostics and host gate/auditor chain.",
    "The exact current persistent phase validator independently accepted the final report and all 167 current build/assembly/linker/contract/hardware input hashes. Final cumulative evidence has 228 passing host tests, strict host/guest checks, portable-target checks and two matching independent five-artifact guest builds with unchanged inputs.",
    "Independently checked 206 source snapshot files, 37 retained reports, 217 commands, 434 raw stdout/stderr streams and 939 distinct SHA bindings, including private boot image entries, firmware variables, raw disks, serial logs and screenshots.",
    "All 17 previous P06 scenarios remain present and passed; 18 additional actual P07 processes cover save/reopen, all five journal interruption points followed by separate fresh recovery and idempotent reopen, and physical filesystem-capacity exhaustion.",
    "Actual save and reopen preserve the exact 6000-byte old payload (CRC32 01ea357b), stable identity, ACL, native settings and registry. Prepare interruption recovers old state; commit/first-home/home recover the complete new state (CRC32 69f67483), and checkpoint recovery observes an already checkpointed new state. The full gate independently audits effective home bytes, metadata and immutable disk regions across each branch.",
    "Capacity commits nine 8192-byte files with zero free blocks and rejects the next operation without changing prior content or leaking allocation. Actual completed P07 guests report eight DMA pages reclaimed. Observed remaining stack is 67616 bytes for save, 71264 for read/recovery and 41824 for capacity on the unchanged 131072-byte stack.",
    "Independent journal failure oracle passed 5136 commit I/O cut and persisted-prefix cases plus 42576 staged partial-page updates, comparing the entire 512KiB test home against exact old/new states and checking poison and byte-identical second reopen.",
    "Independent recovery-interruption oracle passed 972 failure/prefix cases across recovery writes and flushes, including both checkpoint mirrors. The complete committed home is recovered after interruption and a second recovery is byte-idempotent.",
    "Independent ext2 oracle passed 12000 randomized operations including 2040 creates, 1967 writes/gap extensions, 1994 shrinks and 2038 unlinks, with 120 complete remounts. Every live byte and all retired identities were checked.",
    "Independent namespace probes checked all 4096 symmetric sharing-mask combinations and 12000 catalog bit mutations, half with recomputed CRC. 11891 mutations were rejected and 109 structurally accepted mutations caused no panic; accepted changes were not assumed to be corrupt.",
    "Independent mirror-relation differential matrix passed 392 cases against a separate arithmetic/state oracle, kernel recovery and host raw inspection. All three original critic reproductions were rerun successfully against the repaired source.",
    "Twelve consistently rebound gate mutations rejected weaker phase, missing/optional host tests, missing journal/namespace/profile inputs, missing/duplicated guest cases, weakened P07 markers and missing/wrong persistence session bindings. 117 mutations of actual final P07 serial streams were rejected.",
    "Viewed the actual normal, diagnostic and panic screenshots and verified completed H/D/R/P interactions. The visible result remains the protected native diagnostic console; P07 does not establish desktop or GUI capability.",
    "No product source or documentation was edited by this critic. No actionable issue remains from this finite review of the declared P07 profile. The phase owner retains responsibility for closure ledger/docs and subsequent phase activation."
  ],
