    "Review and finite tests do not establish absence of every bug.",
    "Actual persistence qualification uses the pinned q35/TCG single-CPU modern VirtIO block profile. Concurrent storage on SMP, physical controllers, hotplug, IOMMU and real drive power-loss behavior remain unqualified.",
    "The journal is an original bounded 64-page redo format around the existing ext2 development subset, not ext4/JBD2. Flush correctness is an assumption of the block-device contract. CRC32 does not authenticate hostile media rewriting or prevent whole-image rollback.",
    "Persistent access requires one serialized owner with exclusive device/cache ownership. RAM staging and flush are not durable acknowledgement until explicit journal commit; uncertain backend failure poisons live state until validated recovery/remount.",
    "The namespace retains the documented bounded node/handle/key/value/ACE counts, 48KiB ext2 file limit, ASCII-only Windows case folding and lossless UTF-16 spelling. Full Win32/NTFS/SID/hive compatibility, reparse points, alternate streams, mappings, asynchronous notifications and authenticated service/session integration remain later requirements.",
    "Subjects are trusted captured identities at this layer; P08 owns authenticated user/service integration. These tests do not qualify a complete login or permission-management user interface.",
    "Host failure models cover selected operation boundaries, byte prefixes and recovery retries; actual guest interruptions cover the five declared durable checkpoints. They are not exhaustive hardware fault injection.",
    "Stack margins are samples at exercised I/O paths, not a proof of worst-case stack bounds under arbitrary future compiler/source changes.",
    "Source/report hashes establish identity in the trusted local workspace rather than external attestation. The cumulative P00-P10 checkpoint and P11-P15 GUI integration remain future work."
